# Corpus unit sequential-neural-score-estimation/C04 — gap (variance + measurement-validity CQs unmet)
#
# Source: m0/annotations/sequential-neural-score-estimation.yaml C04 (comparative,
# controlled_comparison; corpus pin 62e9b54). Headline: TSNPSE-VP achieves a superior percentage
# of valid (non-NaN) summary statistics on the real-world Pyloric problem, reaching 81% in the
# final (9th) round and exceeding both TSNPE and SNVI at every matched simulation budget below 200k
# (E04, Figure 4c).
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * Two-baseline comparison: nearest-competitor convention takes TSNPE (the direct
#     non-score predecessor) as B, the binding comparand; SNVI is dominated in the same window and
#     stays in nl and refs. S = tsnpse_vp, Q = valid_summary_stats, D = pyloric_budget_le_200k
#     (the "all budgets <= 200k" curve window, 30000 + 8*20000 = 190000 <= 200k). The 81% figure
#     lives in nl.
#   * Two policy-mandatory CQs are annotated unmet-gap, so no complete controlled_comparison is
#     declarable and the claim lands `gap` (E2-style): variance_reported <- CQ3 (a single 9-round
#     run, no seeds / uncertainty band, point percentages only); measurement_validity <- CQ4 (the
#     NaN-imputation -- invalid stats replaced 2 SD below the prior predictive -- is specified only
#     for the TSNPSE run, so cross-method comparability of the valid-% metric is unconfirmed, i.e.
#     valid_measurement(valid_summary_stats, e04) cannot be attested).
#   * Met CQs kept as leaves: baseline_parity <- CQ1 (identical Pyloric simulator, 31 params, 18
#     summary stats, prior, observed data; TSNPE/SNVI named baselines); scope_match (optional) <-
#     CQ2/CQ5 (matched simulation budgets, the <200k window covered by the reported rounds). No
#     numeric baseline values are tabulated in the artifact -- dominance is read from Figure 4c
#     curves, hence the attested premise leaf. Dead ends N07/N09/N11 are rejected sequential-
#     correction designs behind C03 -- no attacks.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact sequential-neural-score-estimation at sha256:67e559ec03eb
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim, stated but not assemblable at corpus-v1's evidential bar --------------

claim c04
  nl      = "TSNPSE-VP achieves a superior percentage of valid summary statistics on the Pyloric problem, reaching 81% in the final round and exceeding both TSNPE and SNVI at every matched simulation budget below 200k"
  formal  = better(tsnpse_vp, tsnpe, valid_summary_stats, pyloric_budget_le_200k)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = reviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves are present ... ------------------------------------------------------------

# Principal premise: the Figure 4c valid-% curves (TSNPSE 81% final round, exceeding TSNPE and
# SNVI across the <200k budget window), attested (read from the figure), folded into refs.
leaf e1 : reports(e04, compares(tsnpse_vp, tsnpe, valid_summary_stats, pyloric_budget_le_200k, favorable))
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/claims.md#C04, logic/experiments.md#E04-Expected-outcome, logic/experiments.md#E04-Baselines, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N14]

leaf e2 : matched_setup(tsnpse_vp, tsnpe, e04)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E04-Setup, logic/experiments.md#E04-Baselines]

leaf e5 : scope_matched(tsnpse_vp, valid_summary_stats, pyloric_budget_le_200k)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E04-Procedure-step-7, logic/experiments.md#E04-Setup]

# --- ... but no complete argument is declarable -------------------------------------------------

# (Intentionally no `arg`: variance_reported(e04) has no honest leaf -- single-run point
# percentages -- and valid_measurement(valid_summary_stats, e04) cannot be attested because the
# NaN-imputation is specified only for TSNPSE, leaving cross-method comparability open. corpus-v1
# makes both mandatory. The claim's complete-support set is empty.)

status c04

